Patch T10 oracles (rung 1b, task T10; gate G5, with amendment 24): protect
the harness that runs the platform contract's conformance suite on winit.

- crates/eng-platform-winit/tests/conformance.rs joins protected.toml and
  .github/CODEOWNERS (amendment 35). It is T10's done-when ("the
  conformance suite passes where a display exists"): it runs
  `conformance::check` on real windows, adds the checks the suite cannot
  make on a desktop (real window handles, a clock that restarts each run,
  twenty timed frames that only the platform's timer can bring, one event
  loop per process, and on Linux the no-display skip and
  ENG_REQUIRE_DISPLAY=1), and holds the skip rule itself. Amendment 24
  protects the suite and the headless harness (t3-oracles.patch); without
  this file as well, making the winit harness skip, or dropping a check
  from it, would leave the suite protected but no longer run on winit.
- No xtask step: acceptance names none for this harness, and `tests`
  runs it.

Base: main with T10's commit and t8-oracles.patch applied; the patches
stack, so apply them in one command, in order:
  git apply docs/rungs/1b/patches/t8-oracles.patch \
            docs/rungs/1b/patches/t10-oracles.patch \
            docs/rungs/1b/patches/t3-oracles.patch
then `cargo xtask quick` and `CI=1 cargo xtask ci --job lint` (docs-check
wants the CODEOWNERS line). Session 17's T10 entry in PROGRESS.md says how
it was tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

